<title>HONG KONG: Wanon interim net returns to profit.</title>
<headline>Wanon interim net returns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   0.57 gain   vs  1.07 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	   vs  nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil	   vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    1.50 profit vs  2.83 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		     63.52	 vs  88.77</p>
<p>    Company name		 Wanon International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  May 1-7</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Wanon International is a telephone maker.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one 1999 warrant for every five shares held. Each warrant will entitle the holder to subscribe for new shares at an initial subscription price of HK$1.03 and will be exercisable at any time from May 26, 1997, until May 31, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
